# MicroCoaching Monorepo — Ownership Rules

This is a `uv` workspace with five members: two services, two shared packages, and one eval harness. Cross-boundary imports are NOT allowed unless listed here.

## Allowed import graph

```
services/platform       → packages/contracts, packages/foundation
services/ai-runtime     → packages/contracts, packages/foundation
eval/rag-eval           → packages/contracts, services/platform
packages/contracts      → (pydantic only)
packages/foundation     → (infra libs only — no business logic)
```

- `services/ai-runtime` **must not** import from `services/platform` and must not touch PostgreSQL, Redis, or ClickHouse.
- `services/platform` **must not** import AI provider SDKs (`google.generativeai`). Talk to ai-runtime via `AIRuntimeClient` instead.
- `packages/foundation` **must not** contain SQLAlchemy models, repositories, or domain logic — only config base classes, logging, HTTP primitives.
- `packages/contracts` is DTOs/enums only. No runtime behavior.

## Where to make a change

| Task | Location |
|------|----------|
| New public route | `services/platform/src/platform_service/api/` |
| New internal AI capability | `services/ai-runtime/src/ai_runtime/api/` + `providers/` |
| Schema change | `infra/alembic/versions/` + `services/platform/src/platform_service/db/models/` |
| Shared DTO | `packages/contracts/src/mc_contracts/` |
| Shared infra helper | `packages/foundation/src/mc_foundation/` |
| Queue consumer | `services/platform/src/platform_service/workers/` |
| RAG eval harness | `eval/src/eval/rag/` |

## Canonical endpoint contract

Route names listed in `README.md` ("Canonical Endpoint Contract") are the contract. Do NOT introduce drifted names (`/coaching/counselling` is canonical; `/counselling`, `/coaching/counsel` are not). When unsure, grep `README.md` for the route prefix before adding a route.
